{"name":"Sweet Angelica","hex":"#e8d08e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"angelica","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tall plant, with hollow stems, genus Angelica, especially garden angelica (Angelica archangelica).","A candied stem of the plant, used to decorate cookies."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angelica"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosemary & Thyme","blocks":[{"text":"Rosemary & Thyme is a British television cosy mystery thriller comedy drama series starring Felicity Kendal and Pam Ferris as gardening detectives Rosemary Boxer and Laura Thyme. The show began on ITV in 2003. The third series ended in August 2007. The theme is murder mysteries in the setting of professional gardening jobs. It was created by Brian Eastman to entertain his wife, Christabel Albery, who is an avid gardener. The show was directed by Brian Farnham, Simon Langton, Tom Clegg and Gwennan Sage. Clive Exton, who helped create the show, contributed 10 of the 22 scripts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a4/Rosemaryandthyme1.jpg/330px-Rosemaryandthyme1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosemary_%26_Thyme"},{"title":"Sweetness","blocks":[{"text":"Sweetness is a basic taste most commonly perceived when eating foods rich in sugar. Sweet tastes are generally regarded as pleasurable. In addition to sugars like sucrose, many other chemical compounds are sweet, including aldehydes, ketones, and sugar alcohols. Some are sweet at very low concentrations, allowing their use as non-caloric sugar substitutes. Such non-sugar sweeteners include saccharin, aspartame, sucralose and stevia. Other compounds, such as miraculin, may alter perception of sweetness itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Strawberry_shortcake.jpg/330px-Strawberry_shortcake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetness"},{"title":"Angelica","blocks":[{"text":"Angelica is a genus of about 90 species of tall biennial and perennial herbs in the family Apiaceae, native to temperate and subarctic regions of the Northern Hemisphere, reaching as far north as Iceland, Sápmi, and Greenland. They grow to 1–3 m tall, with large bipinnate leaves and large compound umbels of white or greenish-white flowers. It shows variations in fruit anatomy, leaf morphology, and subterranean structures. The genes are extremely polymorphic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Gewone_engwortel_R0012880_Plant.JPG/330px-Gewone_engwortel_R0012880_Plant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angelica"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Munden_House%2C_Watford%2C_Hertfordshire-geograph-5190457-by-Robert-Eva.jpg/500px-Munden_House%2C_Watford%2C_Hertfordshire-geograph-5190457-by-Robert-Eva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Munden_House%2C_Watford%2C_Hertfordshire-geograph-5190457-by-Robert-Eva.jpg/1280px-Munden_House%2C_Watford%2C_Hertfordshire-geograph-5190457-by-Robert-Eva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Munden_House%2C_Watford%2C_Hertfordshire-geograph-5190457-by-Robert-Eva.jpg/500px-Munden_House%2C_Watford%2C_Hertfordshire-geograph-5190457-by-Robert-Eva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mu